for small and medium-sized businesses in the United States. The company offers multi-state payroll processing and tax administration; employee benefits programs, including health insurance and retirement plans; workers' compensation insurance and claims management; employment and benefits law compliance; and other HR related services. It also provides a technology platform, an online and mobile tool that allows users to store, view, and manage HR information and administer various HR transactions, such as payroll processing, tax administration and credits, employee onboarding and termination, employee performance, time and attendance, compensation reporting, expense management, and benefits enrollment and administration, as well as incorporated workforce analytics and allows professional employer organization and administrative services offering clients to generate HR data, payroll, compensation, and other custom reports. The company serves clients in various industries, including technology, professional services, financial services, life sciences, and not-for-profit. It sells its solutions through its direct sales organization. TriNet Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1988 and is headquartered in Dublin, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Quinn Simonds | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 298K people. Revenue per employee of $17K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $783 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $217 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 137\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["TriNet Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.0B market cap on $5.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 45% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 37-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $234M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.95\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 28% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Investigates Claims On Behalf of Investors of TriNet Group, Inc. - TNET","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-investigates-claims-on-behalf-of-investors-of-trinet-group-inc---tnet-302938460.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794537720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.447,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"TriNet Group (TNET) Faces A Fresh Valuation Test Following Third Quarter Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-tnet/trinet-group/news/trinet-group-tnet-faces-a-fresh-valuation-test-following-thi","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794256187.688,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.898,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"TriNet Group's (NYSE:TNET) Earnings Offer More Than Meets The Eye","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-tnet/trinet-group/news/trinet-groups-nysetnet-earnings-offer-more-than-meets-the-ey","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793991500.559,"origin":